.TITLE "du"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays disk usage for files and directories. It calculates the space occupied by __filesystem objects__ and helps identify large folders or files.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**du**
Lists the disk usage for all files and directories in the current path.
> 

**du -h**
Displays sizes in human-readable formats like KB, MB, or GB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag

**du -s**
Shows only a total sum for each specified file or directory.
> __-s__ summary flag

**du -d 1**
Limits the display to a specific depth within the directory tree.
> __-d__ depth flag | __1__ depth level

**du -k**
Displays sizes in kilobyte blocks which is the default for many BSD systems.
> __-k__ kilobytes flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combining __du -s -h *__ is a great way to quickly identify which items in a directory are consuming the most space. On macOS, the __-d__ flag is preferred over the Linux __--max-depth__ equivalent.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:df** **mac:ls**

